ts and security challenges=2C and provide analysis that can help in securi=
ng the online world. The pandemic presented a unique opportunity to malici=
ous actors=2C the protection provided by the corporate network and their f=
irewalls had been smashed. Work from home (WFH) has increased the volume=
=2C frequency=2C and scope of cyber attacks. Considering the situation=2C=
 this week's special episode focuses on organizations' security=2C complia=
nce=2C and privacy posture=2C and how WFH has challenged the status quo. L=
isten to our guest speaker security expert Rebecca Wynn=2C Global CISO and=
 Chief Privacy Officer=2C share her experience in transitioning organizati=
ons to a secure WFH model=2C explore the implications of WFH environments=
 & provide insights on some best practices that can help organizations sec=
ure themselves from looming threats.
