                      <span style="display:block;">
                        Welcome to a special edition of the <b>DNS Sonar Report,</b> our weekly cyber <br class="desktop-view">threat intelligence podcast where we dig deeper into the latest cyber <br class="desktop-view">threats and security challenges, and provide analysis that can help in <br class="desktop-view">securing the online world.
                      </span>
                      <span class="middle-content" style="display:block; padding: 30px 0 30px;">
                        The pandemic presented a unique opportunity to malicious actors, the <br class="desktop-view">protection provided by the corporate network and their firewalls had been <br class="desktop-view">smashed. Work from home (WFH) has increased the volume, frequency, <br class="desktop-view">and scope of cyber attacks. Considering the situation, this week's special <br class="desktop-view">episode focuses on organizations' security, compliance, and privacy <br class="desktop-view">posture, and how WFH has challenged the status quo.
                      </span>
                      <span class="last-content" style="display:block; padding: 0 0 40px;">
